      'A carrier of persons for reward must use the utmost care and diligence for their safe carriage, provide everything necessary for that purpose, and exercise a reasonable degree of skill (Civil Code § 2100), and it must provide vehicles safe and fit for their purpose (§ 2101). Anyone who offers to the public to carry persons is a common carrier (§ 2168). California juries are told that a common carrier must use the highest care and the vigilance of a very cautious person, though it does not guarantee its passengers’ safety (CACI No. 902). When the bus belongs to a public agency, the agency answers for its employee’s negligence on the job (Government Code § 815.2), but a written government claim generally must be presented within six months of the injury (§ 911.2), and if the agency rejects it in writing, the lawsuit is generally due within six months of that notice (§ 945.6).',
